<Layout title="Terms of Use — Preview My Post" description="Terms for using the Preview My Post browser-based Instagram preview and crop-checking tool.">
	<article class="legal-page"><span class="eyebrow">Terms</span><h1>Terms of Use</h1><p class="lead">Use Preview My Post as a visual review aid, and verify important content before publishing.</p>
	<h2>Permitted Use</h2><p>You may use the tool to preview content you own or have permission to use. Preview identity fields are for presentation testing only. Do not use the tool to impersonate, deceive, infringe rights, or create misleading endorsements.</p>
	<h2>No Publishing or Platform Access</h2><p>The service does not connect to Instagram, authenticate accounts, publish posts, or use the Meta API. You remain responsible for your content and compliance with applicable laws and platform terms.</p>
	<h2>Estimates, Not Guarantees</h2><p>Previews and warnings are estimates. Interface layouts may differ by account, device, region, software version, or experiment. Verify essential content in the current Instagram application before publishing.</p>
	<h2>Availability</h2><p>The service is provided on an “as available” basis. Features may change as platform layouts, browser capabilities, and the product evolve.</p></article>
</Layout>
